      "description": "Watch Neom SC vs Al Khaleej Saihat highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 3, 2026. The Pro League clash between Neom SC and Al Khaleej Saihat on September 3, 2026, delivered a high-octane encounter filled with tactical intrigue. Fans at the stadium witnessed a match defined by sudden bursts of clinical finishing and intense defensive battles. A Physical Opening Exchange The contest began with both sides testing each other's resolve in the middle of the park. Discipline became an early factor as Abdulmalik Al Oyayari received a yellow card in the 14th minute for a mistimed challenge. As Neom SC began to find their rhythm, the game's physical nature continued, leading to a caution for Kiki Kouyate in the 35th minute. Despite the stop-start nature of the opening half-hour, the breakthrough was looming just around the corner. The Eight-Minute Blitz Everything changed in the 37th minute when the deadlock was finally broken. The clinical Alexandre Lacazette found the back of the net, finishing off a well-placed pass from Haroune Camara . The goal sent the home supporters into a frenzy, and before Al Khaleej could regroup, they were hit again. Just two minutes later, Muhannad Al Saad doubled the advantage, expertly converting a chance created by Amadou Kone . Neom SC refused to take their foot off the gas as the first half drew to a close. In the 45th minute, Amadou Kone turned from provider to scorer. Assisted by Khalil Al Absi , Kone’s strike ensured a dominant lead heading into the interval, capping off a remarkable eight-minute spell that effectively took the game away from the visitors. Tactical Shifts and Late Tension The second half saw a series of tactical adjustments as both managers looked to the bench. Neom SC introduced Angelo Fulgini and Alaa Hajji to maintain control, while Al Khaleej brought on fresh legs like Saleh Al-Amri in hopes of a comeback. However, the hosts' defensive structure remained disciplined throughout the second period. As the clock ticked toward full-time, the intensity boiled over, resulting in late bookings for Khalil Al Absi and Angelo Fulgini . Despite Al Khaleej ’s late efforts to find a consolation goal, the referee’s final whistle after five minutes of stoppage time confirmed a professional performance and a decisive victory for Neom SC ."
